    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">&quot;Target assumptions: The OSEs are the ones responsible for submitting eipdemiological  reports as they are Officier de Surveillance Epidemiologique working under DELR.  Despite ASCP assisting OSEs in this role of surveillance, the latter are the ones reponsible for reporting through MESI on the surveillance cases. There is a total of 364 OSEs (including 13 Departmental, and the rest combining communal and institutional) they all attend the weekly situation room on cases update but they submit a monthly report through MESI.  DELR validates data sent by OSE on a quarterly basis where each are required to bring primary sources of data to be reviewed.  This activity is conducted in each department individually and led by DELR officials.  Proposed denominator is then switch to number of OSE reporting instead of institutions.  Not all insititution reports go through MESI and we would not be able to report on that, whereas reporting by OSE is secured through MESI and can be Extracted each period.

Numerator: The number of OSE sending community reports integrated into the DHIS2 tracker/MESI platform
Denominator: Total number of OSE due to report through MESI (364). The MESI information system is used to collect surveillance data including for Malaria, HIV and TB. A total of 1033 public and private sector health institutions are identified by the MSPP to report monthly to this system via the 364 OSEs installed in the various municipalities of the country
Measurement methods: TBD.</narrative>
